  "finalText": "I restocked the 2 cancelled USB-C Hubs. The verifier's issue was right.\n\n- **Check before changing:** O-3001 L3 was cancelled and refunded 13800 to the card. P-HUB stock was 8. The order doesn't mark L3 as backordered, and nothing else in the data shows it was. Other open orders show unshipped lines as plain \"pending\", so my earlier backorder reading was only a guess. The domain rule says cancelled lines that had stock set aside go back into stock. The 2 hubs never left the warehouse, so I put them back.\n- **Fix:** I restocked 2 × P-HUB against O-3001, with the reason citing the cancellation of L3. Stock went from 8 to 10.\n- **Left alone:** The refunds and the order record were already correct. L3 was refunded to the card. L1 and L2 were refunded as store credit, because they shipped outside the 30-day window. Priya's balance is 55300 and the order shows 68600 refunded of 68600 paid. I didn't restock the dock (P-DOC) or monitor (P-MON). They go back into stock only once the warehouse receives them, and nothing shows they have arrived.\n- **If the line was backordered:** If the warehouse says L3 was actually backordered, the 2 hubs should come back out of stock.",
